 "title": "Splatting the Gaussians into Blender",
 "link": "https://code.blender.org/2026/10/splatting-the-gaussians-into-blender/",
 "raw": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd\">\n<?xml encoding=\"utf-8\"?><html><body><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In Blender 5.3, we are introducing initial support for 3D Gaussian splats! This enables importing, editing, and rendering of fast, high-quality scene captures.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A lot of groundwork has been done to integrate 3D Gaussian splats (gsplats) into Blender natively, and we&rsquo;ll continue to refine our implementation in upcoming releases. In this post, we&rsquo;ll outline how to use gsplats, how they&rsquo;re implemented in Blender, and what the current limitations are.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-8f761849 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><video height=\"1080\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 1920 / 1080;\" width=\"1920\" autoplay controls loop muted src=\"https://code.blender.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Start-dogwalk_rotate.mp4\" playsinline></video><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A photoscan of <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3775050/DOGWALK/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3775050/DOGWALK/\">DOGWALK</a> assets as physical objects, rendered as Gaussian splats in Blender 5.3</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\"><video height=\"1080\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 1920 / 1080;\" width=\"1920\" autoplay controls loop muted src=\"https://code.blender.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Start-overgrown_rotate.mp4\" playsinline></video><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A 3D scene from <a href=\"https://studio.blender.org/projects/overgrown/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https://studio.blender.org/projects/overgrown/\">OVERGROWN</a>, rendered as Gaussian splats in Blender 5.3</figcaption></figure>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary><strong>What are Gaussian splats?</strong></summary>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">3D Gaussian splatting is a recent rendering technique in which sets of photos are turned into a specific 3D reconstruction. This doesn&rsquo;t produce a mesh, but a radiance field made of many tiny Gaussian blobs. It&rsquo;s similar to a point cloud, but able to represent more varied structures. Gsplats can describe complex scenes with materials, lighting, transparency, hair, and fine details, all in a single object.</p>\n</details>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:57px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<a href=\"#getting-started\" class=\"is-heading-anchor\"><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"getting-started\">Getting Started</h2></a>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">"
}
